# Module expected-refusal fixture: a zero step is refused, never
# silently an identity. The family refuses non_positive_step. Against
# the pre-family scalar wrappers this program would NOT refuse (the
# old modules returned y unchanged) — that gap is the failure-first
# case this fixture closes.
# Expected outcome: exits nonzero with `non_positive_step`.
# Run: emath test tests/fixtures/modules/evolution_refuse_zero_step.emath

use analysis.evolution.one_step

emath function ZeroStepRefuses:
    inputs:
        unused: Int
    outputs:
        result: SimState
    definitions:
        decay_f = function t in Rat: function s in SimState: SimState: {t: t, y: [0 / 1 - s.y[0]]}
        result = family_euler_step(decay_f, 0 / 1, SimState: {t: 0 / 1, y: [1 / 1]})
    tests:
        example <zero_step>:
            given unused = 0
            expect result == result
